## Why This Is Asked
Tests DP over subsequences with a fixed length and pairwise costs, plus explicit reconstruction. It moves beyond contiguous partitions by requiring last-step linkage through prior picks.

## Key Concepts
- Subsequence DP with fixed length
- Min-over-predecessor recurrence
- Path reconstruction via parent pointers
- Time/space trade-offs and practical optimizations

## Code Example
```javascript
function solve(A, m){
  const n=A.length;
  const dp=Array.from({length:n},()=>Array(m+1).fill(Infinity));
  const par=Array.from({length:n},()=>Array(m+1).fill(-1));
  for(let i=0;i<n;i++) dp[i][1]=0;
  for(let t=2;t<=m;t++){
    for(let i=t-1;i<n;i++){
      for(let j=t-2;j<i;j++){
        const c=dp[j][t-1]+Math.abs(A[i]-A[j]);
        if(c<dp[i][t]){ dp[i][t]=c; par[i][t]=j; }
      }
    }
  }
  let best=Infinity,bestI=-1;
  for(let i=m-1;i<n;i++){ if(dp[i][m]<best){ best=dp[i][m]; bestI=i; } }
  const path=[];
  let cur=bestI, t=m;
  while(t>=1){
    path.push(cur);
    cur=par[cur][t];
    t--;
  }
  path.reverse();
  return {cost:best, indices:path};
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests the ability to design a DP with two choices per step (1- or 2-length blocks), plus reconstruction and complexity awareness.

## Key Concepts

- DP with two dimensions (i, t)
- Transitions for 1-length and 2-length blocks
- Reconstruction via parent pointers
- Time/space trade-offs and potential optimization

## Code Example

```javascript
function maxValueBlocks(A, k){
  const n = A.length;
  const NEG = -1e15;
  const dp = Array.from({length: n+1}, ()=> Array(k+1).fill(NEG));
  const take = Array.from({length: n+1}, ()=> Array(k+1).fill(0));
  dp[0][0] = 0;
  for(let i=1;i<=n;i++){
    for(let t=1;t<=k;t++){
      // 1-length block ending at i-1
      if(dp[i-1][t-1] !== NEG){
        const val = dp[i-1][t-1] + A[i-1];
        if(val > dp[i][t]){ dp[i][t] = val; take[i][t] = 1; }
      }
      // 2-length block ending at i-1
      if(i>=2 && dp[i-2][t-1] !== NEG){
        const val = dp[i-2][t-1] + A[i-2] + A[i-1];
        if(val > dp[i][t]){ dp[i][t] = val; take[i][t] = 2; }
      }
    }
  }
  // reconstruction would trace back from (n, k)
  return dp[n][k];
}
```

